<article class="env-corollary" id="EB9835">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/EB9835">Corollary <span data-tag="EB9835">2.1.2.7</span>.</a> Let $i: A \rightarrow A'$ be left-anodyne, and let $j: B \rightarrow B'$ be a cofibration. Then the induced map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[ (A \times B') \coprod _{A \times B} (A' \times B) \rightarrow A' \times B' \]
</div>
  <p> is left-anodyne. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from Proposition <a href="/tag/BE5D0B" data-tag="BE5D0B">2.3.2.1</a>, which characterizes the class of left-anodyne maps as the class generated by $A_3$ (which is stable under smash products with any cofibration). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>